abstract: >-
  Heritage Moisture & Salt Lab is a reproducible computational framework
  for climate-to-material exposure modelling in porous archaeological
  heritage. The software implements a reduced one-dimensional,
  thickness-averaged heat, moisture, and dissolved sulfate transport
  framework for long-duration historical and future climate simulations.
  The publication release includes the scientific model core,
  long-duration execution and checkpoint/resume components,
  AnalysisBridge for scientific output reduction and audit,
  numerical verification materials, HAMSTAD Benchmark 2 evidence,
  climate-disaggregation validation, lower-boundary sensitivity analysis,
  frozen study configuration, and reproducibility documentation.
  The framework was developed and demonstrated using a 21-case
  historical and CMIP6 future-climate ensemble for Mohenjo-daro,
  Pakistan. It is intended for auditable climate-to-material exposure
  analysis and is not presented as a fully site-calibrated mechanical
  damage model.
